    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0719" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00 Revolutions/61: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-23T11:00:00-07:00">January 23,
                            1932—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. International Railway authorities have just informed me that Communists
                    attacked and are in possession of Sonsonate; they failed in attempt on
                    Ahuachapán. Salvadoran Government sending troop[s] but English railway torn up
                    so they cannot reach Sonsonate before noon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
